t)$ infected with the pest is jointly proportional to the number of trees that are infected at time $t,$ measured in months,  and the number of uninfected trees. If the constant of proportionality is $0.2,$ which differential equation could be used to model $P(t)?$" 13194139534918 true] [17592186319758 1113 #uuid "536cae2e-8257-53cb-8c63-c22406092855" 13194139534918 true] [17592186319758 1145 "Since the growth rate of infected trees is *jointly* proportional to the number of trees that are infected at time $t,$ and the number of uninfected trees, the number of infected trees follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.2,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=300.$ Therefore, the number of trees that are infected is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.2P(300-P).\n$$" 13194139534918 true] [17592186319759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319760 13194139534918 true] [17592186319759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319761 13194139534918 true] [17592186319759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319762 13194139534918 true] [17592186319759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319763 13194139534918 true] [17592186319759 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319764 13194139534918 true] [17592186319759 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534918 true] [17592186319759 1041 "selection" 13194139534918 true] [17592186319759 1104 #edb/ref 17592186319763 13194139534918 true] [17592186319759 1110 #uuid "453ecb49-37df-542f-8f0b-94f362228a8d" 13194139534918 true] [17592186319760 1034 "\\frac{dP}{dt}=300P(0.2-P)" 13194139534918 true] [17592186319760 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534918 true] [17592186319760 1111 #uuid "eb113e85-eb3c-5f6a-9feb-a1213b151d63" 13194139534918 true] [17592186319761 1034 "\\frac{dP}{dt}=300P(0.2+P)" 13194139534918 true] [17592186319761 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534918 true] [17592186319761 1111 #uu